/-!
# Modules induced from a character of a Lie subalgebra

Let `B` be a Lie subalgebra of a Lie algebra `L` over a commutative ring `R`, and let
`χ : B → R` be a character of `B`. The elements `ι x - χ x` of `U(L)`, for `x : B`, generate a
left ideal of `U(L)`, and the quotient of `U(L)` by it is the induced module
`U(L) ⊗_{U(B)} R_χ`, presented without a tensor product over the noncommutative ring `U(B)`. This
file proves that the left ideal is **proper** as soon as `B` has a complement in `L` and both `B`
and the complement are free; over a field this holds for every Lie subalgebra. In other words, the
induced module is nonzero.

When the complement is itself a Lie subalgebra `A`, the induced module is moreover a **free
`U(A)`-module of rank one** on the class of `1`: every element of `U(L)` is congruent to an element
of `U(A)` modulo the left ideal, and an element of `U(A)` lying in the left ideal is zero. For a
semisimple Lie algebra, its Borel subalgebra `𝔟` and the opposite nilradical `n⁻`, this is the
freeness of the Verma module over `U(n⁻)`.

The input is the freeness half of the Poincaré--Birkhoff--Witt theorem relative to a subalgebra:
`U(L)` is a free right `U(B)`-module on the ordered monomials in a basis of a complement of `B`.
For a semisimple Lie algebra and its Borel subalgebra this is what makes Verma modules nonzero.
The spanning half needs no basis: it only uses that `U(L) = U(A) · U(B)` when `A` and `B` span
`L`, and that every element `r` of `U(B)` is congruent to the scalar `χ r`.

The same coordinates control the PBW filtration of the induced module. Modulo the left ideal and
filtration degree `d - 1`, filtration degree `d` is spanned by the ordered monomials of degree `d`
in a basis of a complement of `B`, and over a field, ordered monomials of degree `d` in a linearly
independent family whose span meets `B` only in zero stay linearly independent. This is the
identification of the associated graded of `U(L) ⊗_{U(B)} R_χ` with the symmetric algebra of
`L / B`, read degreewise.
It gives the behaviour of induced relations along a downward-directed family of Lie subalgebras
`B i` with compatible characters: the left ideals they generate intersect in the left ideal
generated by the intersection of the `B i`. An element of filtration degree `d` in every left
ideal has, modulo the intersection's left ideal, a top-degree part built from finitely many basis
vectors of a complement of the intersection. Their span is finite-dimensional, so it meets some
`B i` only in zero, and independence for that `B i` kills the top-degree part.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap_ne_top_of_isCompl`: over a
  nontrivial commutative ring, if `B` has a complement and both are free, the left ideal generated
  by `ι x - χ x` is proper.
* `TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap_ne_top`: over a field, the same
  holds for every Lie subalgebra.
* `UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.map_sub_algebraMap_lift_mem_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap`:
  every `r` in `U(B)` is congruent to `χ r` modulo the left ideal.
* `TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.exists_sub_map_mem_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap`: if the Lie
  subalgebras `A` and `B` span `L`, every element of `U(L)` is congruent to one of `U(A)`.
* `TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.map_mem_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap_iff_of_isCompl`: if the
  Lie subalgebra `A` is a complement of `B` and both are free, an element of `U(A)` lies in the left
  ideal only if it is zero.
* `TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι_sub_algebraMap_mem_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap_iff`:
  over a field, `ι x - a` lies in the left ideal exactly when `x` lies in `B` and `a = χ x`.
* `LieAlgebra.LieCharacter.pbwFiltration_le_span_pbwMonomial_sup`: modulo the left ideal
  and lower filtration degree, the degree-`d` complement monomials span filtration degree `d`.
* `LieAlgebra.LieCharacter.linearIndepOn_mkQ_pbwMonomial`: over a field, degree-`d`
  monomials in a linearly independent family whose span meets `B` only in zero stay independent
  modulo the left ideal and lower filtration degree.
* `TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.iInf_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap`: over a field, the left
  ideals induced along a downward-directed family of Lie subalgebras intersect in the left ideal
  induced from their intersection.

## Implementation notes

Choose an ordered basis of `L` that lists a basis of the complement `A` before a basis of `B`. By
PBW its ordered monomials form a basis of `U(L)`, and each of them factors as an ordered monomial
in the basis of `A` times the image of an ordered monomial of `U(B)`. The linear form on `U(L)`
that reads off the coefficient of a fixed `A`-monomial and applies `χ` to it is then right
`U(B)`-semilinear along `χ`, so it kills the left ideal. The form attached to the empty monomial
sends `1` to `1`, which gives properness; when `A` is a Lie subalgebra, the forms attached to all
monomials restrict on `U(A)` to its PBW coordinates, which gives freeness. Rather than building
the right `U(B)`-module structure, the file defines these linear forms directly on the PBW basis.

## References

* J. E. Humphreys, *Introduction to Lie Algebras and Representation Theory*, GTM 9, §17.4
  and §20.3.
* J. Dixmier, *Enveloping Algebras*, Chapter 5, for induced modules and their PBW filtration.
-/

public section

namespace TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra

open LieAlgebra Module

attribute [local instance 100] LieRing.ofAssociativeRing

universe u v w₁ w₂

variable {R : Type u} {L : Type v} [CommRing R] [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra R L]

local notation "U" => _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra R L

section Adapted

variable (B : LieSubalgebra R L) {A : Submodule R L} (hA : IsCompl A (B : Submodule R L))
  {ιA : Type w₁} {ιB : Type w₂} (bA : Basis ιA R A) (bB : Basis ιB R B)

variable [LinearOrder ιA] [LinearOrder ιB]

/-- The ordered monomial in the basis of the complement with exponent vector `α`. -/
private noncomputable def complementMonomial (α : ιA →₀ ℕ) : U :=
  pbwMonomial R L (fun i ↦ (bA i : L)) (α.toMultiset.sort (· ≤ ·))

variable (χ : LieCharacter R B)

/-- The linear form on `U(L)` reading off the coefficient of the complement monomial with
exponents `α` in the free right `U(B)`-module structure, and applying the character `χ` to it. -/
private noncomputable def characterForm (α : ιA →₀ ℕ) : U →ₗ[R] R :=
  (B.relativePBWBasis hA bA bB).constr R fun n ↦
    if n.1 = α then
      _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lift R χ (bB.pbwBasis n.2)
    else 0

private theorem _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.characterForm_complementMonomial_mul
    (α α' : ιA →₀ ℕ) (y : _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra R B) :
    characterForm B hA bA bB χ α (complementMonomial bA α' * map R B.incl y) =
      if α' = α then _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lift R χ y else 0 := by
  have hlin := bB.pbwBasis.ext (f₁ := characterForm B hA bA bB χ α ∘ₗ
      LinearMap.mulLeft R (complementMonomial bA α') ∘ₗ (map R B.incl).toLinearMap)
    (f₂ := if α' = α then (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lift R χ).toLinearMap else 0)
    fun β ↦ by
      simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, AlgHom.toLinearMap_apply, LinearMap.mulLeft_apply]
      rw [complementMonomial, ← LieSubalgebra.relativePBWBasis_apply B hA, characterForm,
        Basis.constr_basis]
      split_ifs <;> simp
  have hy := LinearMap.congr_fun hlin y
  split_ifs at hy ⊢ <;> simpa using hy

/-- The character form is right `U(B)`-semilinear along the character `χ`. -/
private theorem _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.characterForm_mul_map (α : ιA →₀ ℕ) (u : U)
    (r : _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra R B) :
    characterForm B hA bA bB χ α (u * map R B.incl r) =
      characterForm B hA bA bB χ α u * _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lift R χ r := by
  have hlin := (B.relativePBWBasis hA bA bB).ext
    (f₁ := characterForm B hA bA bB χ α ∘ₗ LinearMap.mulRight R (map R B.incl r))
    (f₂ := _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lift R χ r • characterForm B hA bA bB χ α)
    fun n ↦ by
      rcases n with ⟨α', β⟩
      rw [LieSubalgebra.relativePBWBasis_apply, ← complementMonomial]
      simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.mulRight_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply,
        mul_assoc, ← map_mul,
        _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.characterForm_complementMonomial_mul, smul_eq_mul]
      split_ifs <;> simp [mul_comm]
  simpa [mul_comm] using LinearMap.congr_fun hlin u

/-- The character form of index `α` sends `1` to `1` if `α = 0` and to `0` otherwise. -/
private theorem characterForm_one_apply (α : ιA →₀ ℕ) :
    characterForm B hA bA bB χ α 1 = if (0 : ιA →₀ ℕ) = α then 1 else 0 := by
  simpa [complementMonomial] using
    _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.characterForm_complementMonomial_mul B hA bA bB χ α 0 1

/-- Every character form vanishes on the left ideal generated by the elements `ι x - χ x`. -/
private theorem characterForm_eq_zero_of_mem_span (α : ιA →₀ ℕ) {s : U}
    (hs : s ∈ Submodule.span U (Set.range fun x : B ↦
      _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (x : L) - algebraMap R U (χ x))) :
    characterForm B hA bA bB χ α s = 0 := by
  suffices key : ∀ v : U, characterForm B hA bA bB χ α (v * s) = 0 by simpa using key 1
  induction hs using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem s hs =>
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hs
    intro v
    dsimp only
    have hx : _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (x : L) - algebraMap R U (χ x) =
        map R B.incl (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R x -
          algebraMap R (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra R B) (χ x)) := by
      rw [map_sub, map_ι, AlgHom.commutes, LieSubalgebra.coe_incl]
    rw [hx, _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.characterForm_mul_map]
    simp
  | zero => simp
  | add s t _ _ hs ht => simp [mul_add, hs, ht]
  | smul a s _ hs =>
    intro v
    rw [smul_eq_mul, ← mul_assoc]
    exact hs _

include hA bA bB in
/-- The left ideal generated by `ι x - χ x` is proper, given ordered bases of `B` and of a
complement. -/
private theorem span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap_ne_top_of_basis [Nontrivial R] :
    Submodule.span U (Set.range fun x : B ↦
      _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (x : L) - algebraMap R U (χ x)) ≠ ⊤ := by
  intro htop
  have h1 := characterForm_eq_zero_of_mem_span B hA bA bB χ 0 (htop ▸ Submodule.mem_top (x := 1))
  rw [characterForm_one_apply, ite_eq_left rfl] at h1
  exact one_ne_zero h1

/-- On the image of `U(A)` for a Lie subalgebra `A` complementing `B`, the character form of
index `α` is the coefficient of the ordered monomial of exponents `α`. -/
private theorem _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.characterForm_map_incl
    {A : LieSubalgebra R L}
    (hA : IsCompl (A : Submodule R L) (B : Submodule R L)) (bA : Basis ιA R A) (α : ιA →₀ ℕ)
    (y : _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra R A) :
    characterForm B hA bA bB χ α (map R A.incl y) = bA.pbwBasis.repr y α := by
  have hlin := bA.pbwBasis.ext
    (f₁ := characterForm B hA bA bB χ α ∘ₗ (map R A.incl).toLinearMap)
    (f₂ := Finsupp.lapply α ∘ₗ bA.pbwBasis.repr.toLinearMap) fun α' ↦ by
      have hmon : map R A.incl (bA.pbwBasis α') =
          complementMonomial (A := (A : Submodule R L)) bA α' * map R B.incl 1 := by
        rw [map_one, mul_one, complementMonomial, Basis.pbwBasis_apply, map_pbwMonomial]
        simp only [pbwMonomial_def, List.map_map, Function.comp_def, LieSubalgebra.coe_incl]
      simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, AlgHom.toLinearMap_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe,
        Basis.repr_self, Finsupp.lapply_apply, Finsupp.single_apply]
      rw [hmon, _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.characterForm_complementMonomial_mul, map_one]
  exact LinearMap.congr_fun hlin y

/-- The character form of index `α` sends the generator `ι (bA j)` to `1` if `α` is the exponent
vector of `j` and to `0` otherwise. -/
private theorem characterForm_ι_basis (α : ιA →₀ ℕ) (j : ιA) :
    characterForm B hA bA bB χ α (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (bA j : L)) =
      if Finsupp.single j 1 = α then 1 else 0 := by
  have hmon : complementMonomial bA (Finsupp.single j 1) * map R B.incl 1 =
      _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (bA j : L) := by
    simp [complementMonomial, pbwMonomial_cons, pbwMonomial_nil]
  rw [← hmon, _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.characterForm_complementMonomial_mul, map_one]

/-- On a degree-one element `ι w + r` with `w` in the complement, the character form of index `0`
reads off the scalar `r`. -/
private theorem characterForm_zero_ι_add_algebraMap (w : A) (r : R) :
    characterForm B hA bA bB χ 0 (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (w : L) +
      algebraMap R U r) = r := by
  have hι : characterForm B hA bA bB χ 0 ∘ₗ
      (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R).toLinearMap ∘ₗ A.subtype = 0 :=
    bA.ext fun j ↦ by
      simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, Submodule.subtype_apply, LieHom.coe_toLinearMap,
        characterForm_ι_basis, LinearMap.zero_apply]
      simp
  have hw := LinearMap.congr_fun hι w
  simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, Submodule.subtype_apply, LieHom.coe_toLinearMap,
    LinearMap.zero_apply] at hw
  rw [map_add, hw, Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one, map_smul, characterForm_one_apply]
  simp

/-- On a degree-one element `ι w + r` with `w` in the complement, the character form of the
exponent vector of `j` reads off the `j`-th coordinate of `w`. -/
private theorem characterForm_single_ι_add_algebraMap (j : ιA) (w : A) (r : R) :
    characterForm B hA bA bB χ (Finsupp.single j 1)
      (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (w : L) + algebraMap R U r) = bA.repr w j := by
  have hι : characterForm B hA bA bB χ (Finsupp.single j 1) ∘ₗ
      (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R).toLinearMap ∘ₗ A.subtype =
        Finsupp.lapply j ∘ₗ bA.repr.toLinearMap :=
    bA.ext fun i ↦ by
      simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, Submodule.subtype_apply, LieHom.coe_toLinearMap,
        characterForm_ι_basis, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, Basis.repr_self, Finsupp.lapply_apply]
      simp [Finsupp.single_apply, Finsupp.single_left_inj one_ne_zero]
  have hw := LinearMap.congr_fun hι w
  simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, Submodule.subtype_apply, LieHom.coe_toLinearMap,
    LinearEquiv.coe_coe, Finsupp.lapply_apply] at hw
  rw [map_add, hw, Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one, map_smul, characterForm_one_apply]
  simp [(Finsupp.single_ne_zero.2 one_ne_zero).symm]

/-- The ordered complement monomial with exponent vector `α` has PBW filtration degree at most the
total degree of `α`. -/
private theorem complementMonomial_mem_pbwFiltration (α : ιA →₀ ℕ) :
    complementMonomial bA α ∈ pbwFiltration R L α.degree := by
  rw [complementMonomial]
  simpa only [Multiset.length_sort, Finsupp.card_toMultiset_eq_degree] using
    pbwMonomial_mem_pbwFiltration R L (fun i ↦ (bA i : L)) (α.toMultiset.sort (· ≤ ·))

/-- The character form of index `α` sends the complement monomial of `α'` to `1` if `α' = α` and
to `0` otherwise. -/
private theorem characterForm_complementMonomial (α α' : ιA →₀ ℕ) :
    characterForm B hA bA bB χ α (complementMonomial bA α') = if α' = α then 1 else 0 := by
  simpa using
    _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.characterForm_complementMonomial_mul B hA bA bB χ α α' 1

/-- A character form whose index has total degree greater than `k` vanishes in PBW filtration
degree `k`. -/
private theorem characterForm_eq_zero_of_mem_pbwFiltration {α : ιA →₀ ℕ} {k : ℕ}
    (hk : k < α.degree) {s : U} (hs : s ∈ pbwFiltration R L k) :
    characterForm B hA bA bB χ α s = 0 := by
  rw [LieSubalgebra.mem_pbwFiltration_iff_relativePBWBasis_repr B hA bA bB] at hs
  rw [← (B.relativePBWBasis hA bA bB).linearCombination_repr s, Finsupp.linearCombination_apply,
    map_finsuppSum]
  refine Finset.sum_eq_zero fun p hp ↦ ?_
  obtain ⟨α', β⟩ := p
  have hdeg := hs _ hp
  dsimp only at hdeg ⊢
  have hne : α' ≠ α := by rintro rfl; omega
  rw [LieSubalgebra.relativePBWBasis_apply, ← complementMonomial]
  simp [_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.characterForm_complementMonomial_mul, hne]

/-- A character form whose index has total degree `d` vanishes below filtration degree `d`. -/
private theorem characterForm_eq_zero_of_mem_pbwFiltrationPrevious {α : ιA →₀ ℕ} {s : U}
    (hs : s ∈ pbwFiltrationPrevious R L α.degree) : characterForm B hA bA bB χ α s = 0 := by
  rcases hd : α.degree with _ | k
  · rw [hd, pbwFiltrationPrevious_zero, Submodule.mem_bot] at hs
    rw [hs, map_zero]
  · rw [hd, pbwFiltrationPrevious_succ] at hs
    exact characterForm_eq_zero_of_mem_pbwFiltration B hA bA bB χ (by omega) hs

end Adapted

section Induced

variable (B : LieSubalgebra R L) (χ : LieCharacter R B)

/-- **`U(B)` acts on the canonical generator through the character.** For every `r` in `U(B)`, the
image of `r` in `U(L)` is congruent to the scalar `χ r` modulo the left ideal generated by the
elements `ι x - χ x`, for `x : B`. In the induced module `U(L) ⊗_{U(B)} R_χ` this says that `r`
acts on the canonical generator by `χ r`. -/
theorem _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.map_sub_algebraMap_lift_mem_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap
    (r : _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra R B) :
    map R B.incl r - algebraMap R U (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lift R χ r) ∈
      Submodule.span U (Set.range fun x : B ↦
        _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (x : L) - algebraMap R U (χ x)) := by
  induction r using induction_ι with
  | ι x =>
    rw [map_ι, _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lift_ι_apply]
    exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨x, rfl⟩
  | algebraMap r => simp
  | add a b ha hb =>
    convert add_mem ha hb using 1
    simp only [map_add]
    abel
  | mul a b ha hb =>
    -- `a b - χ(a) χ(b) = a (b - χ(b)) + χ(b) (a - χ(a))`
    convert add_mem (Submodule.smul_mem _ (map R B.incl a) hb)
      (Submodule.smul_of_tower_mem _ (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lift R χ b) ha) using 1
    simp only [map_mul, smul_eq_mul, mul_sub, Algebra.smul_def,
      ← Algebra.commutes (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lift R χ b) (map R B.incl a)]
    rw [← map_mul (algebraMap R U), ← map_mul (algebraMap R U),
      mul_comm (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lift R χ a)]
    abel

variable {B} in
/-- **The induced module is spanned by the image of `U(A)`** when the Lie subalgebras `A` and `B`
together span `L`: every element of `U(L)` is congruent to an element of `U(A)` modulo the left
ideal generated by the elements `ι x - χ x`, for `x : B`. In the induced module
`U(L) ⊗_{U(B)} R_χ` this says that the canonical generator generates it over `U(A)`. -/
theorem exists_sub_map_mem_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap {A : LieSubalgebra R L}
    (hAB : (A : Submodule R L) ⊔ (B : Submodule R L) = ⊤) (u : U) :
    ∃ y : _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra R A,
      u - map R A.incl y ∈ Submodule.span U (Set.range fun x : B ↦
        _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (x : L) - algebraMap R U (χ x)) := by
  set I := Submodule.span U (Set.range fun x : B ↦
    _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (x : L) - algebraMap R U (χ x))
  -- The elements congruent to an element of `U(A)` contain every product `U(A) · U(B)`.
  have htop : I.restrictScalars R ⊔ LinearMap.range (map R A.incl).toLinearMap = ⊤ := by
    rw [eq_top_iff, ← envelopingSubalgebra_mul_envelopingSubalgebra_eq_top hAB, Submodule.mul_le]
    intro m hm n hn
    obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := (mem_envelopingSubalgebra_iff R).mp ((Subalgebra.mem_toSubmodule _).mp hm)
    obtain ⟨r, rfl⟩ := (mem_envelopingSubalgebra_iff R).mp ((Subalgebra.mem_toSubmodule _).mp hn)
    have hsplit : map R A.incl y * map R B.incl r =
        map R A.incl y * (map R B.incl r -
          algebraMap R U (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lift R χ r)) +
          map R A.incl (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lift R χ r • y) := by
      rw [mul_sub, map_smul, Algebra.smul_def, Algebra.commutes, sub_add_cancel]
    rw [hsplit]
    exact Submodule.add_mem_sup (Submodule.smul_mem I _
      (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.map_sub_algebraMap_lift_mem_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap
        B χ r))
      (LinearMap.mem_range_self _ _)
  obtain ⟨i, hi, w, ⟨y, rfl⟩, hu⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.mp (htop ▸ Submodule.mem_top (x := u))
  exact ⟨y, by simpa [← hu] using hi⟩

variable {B} in
/-- **The image of `U(A)` meets the induced relations only in zero** when the Lie subalgebra `A`
is a complement of `B` and both are free: an element of `U(A)` whose image lies in the left
ideal generated by the elements `ι x - χ x`, for `x : B`, is zero. Together with
`TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.exists_sub_map_mem_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap` this says
that the induced module `U(L) ⊗_{U(B)} R_χ` is a free `U(A)`-module of rank one on its canonical
generator. -/
theorem map_mem_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap_iff_of_isCompl {A : LieSubalgebra R L}
    (hAB : IsCompl (A : Submodule R L) (B : Submodule R L)) [Module.Free R A] [Module.Free R B]
    {y : _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra R A} :
    map R A.incl y ∈ Submodule.span U (Set.range fun x : B ↦
      _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (x : L) - algebraMap R U (χ x)) ↔ y = 0 := by
  refine ⟨fun hy ↦ ?_, fun hy ↦ hy ▸ by simp⟩
  let _ : LinearOrder (Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex R A) := IsWellOrder.linearOrder WellOrderingRel
  let _ : LinearOrder (Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex R B) := IsWellOrder.linearOrder WellOrderingRel
  refine (Module.Free.chooseBasis R A).pbwBasis.repr.injective (Finsupp.ext fun α ↦ ?_)
  rw [← _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.characterForm_map_incl B
      (Module.Free.chooseBasis R B) χ hAB,
    characterForm_eq_zero_of_mem_span B hAB _ _ χ α hy, map_zero, Finsupp.zero_apply]

variable {B} in
/-- **Degree-one elements of the induced relations.** If the Lie subalgebra `B` has a complement
and both are free, then `ι x - a` lies in the left ideal generated by the elements `ι y - χ y`, for
`y : B`, exactly when `x` lies in `B` and `a = χ x`. In the induced module `U(L) ⊗_{U(B)} R_χ`
this says that the map `L × R → U(L) ⊗_{U(B)} R_χ`, `(x, a) ↦ (ι x + a) · 1`, has kernel the
graph of `-χ`. -/
theorem ι_sub_algebraMap_mem_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap_iff_of_isCompl {A : Submodule R L}
    (hA : IsCompl A (B : Submodule R L)) [Module.Free R A] [Module.Free R B] {x : L} {a : R} :
    _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R x - algebraMap R U a ∈
        Submodule.span U (Set.range fun y : B ↦
          _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (y : L) - algebraMap R U (χ y)) ↔
      ∃ y : B, (y : L) = x ∧ χ y = a := by
  refine ⟨fun h ↦ ?_, ?_⟩
  · let _ : LinearOrder (Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex R A) :=
      IsWellOrder.linearOrder WellOrderingRel
    let _ : LinearOrder (Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex R B) :=
      IsWellOrder.linearOrder WellOrderingRel
    let bA := Module.Free.chooseBasis R A
    let bB := Module.Free.chooseBasis R B
    obtain ⟨w, hw, y, hy, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.1 (hA.sup_eq_top ▸ Submodule.mem_top (x := x))
    -- Subtracting the relation of `y` leaves `ι w + (χ y - a)` with `w` in the complement.
    have hrel : _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R ((⟨w, hw⟩ : A) : L) +
        algebraMap R U (χ ⟨y, hy⟩ - a) ∈ Submodule.span U (Set.range fun y : B ↦
          _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (y : L) - algebraMap R U (χ y)) := by
      convert sub_mem h (Submodule.subset_span ⟨⟨y, hy⟩, rfl⟩) using 1
      simp only [map_add, map_sub]
      abel
    have h0 := characterForm_eq_zero_of_mem_span B hA bA bB χ 0 hrel
    rw [characterForm_zero_ι_add_algebraMap] at h0
    have hw0 : (⟨w, hw⟩ : A) = 0 := bA.repr.injective <| Finsupp.ext fun j ↦ by
      have hj := characterForm_eq_zero_of_mem_span B hA bA bB χ (Finsupp.single j 1) hrel
      rw [characterForm_single_ι_add_algebraMap] at hj
      simpa using hj
    have hw_zero : w = 0 := congrArg Subtype.val hw0
    refine ⟨⟨y, hy⟩, ?_, sub_eq_zero.1 h0⟩
    simp [hw_zero]
  · rintro ⟨y, rfl, rfl⟩
    exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨y, rfl⟩

variable {B} in
/-- **Ordered complement monomials span the induced module degreewise.** Let `A` be a complement
of a free Lie subalgebra `B` with an ordered basis `bA`. Modulo the left ideal generated by the
elements `ι x - χ x`, for `x : B`, and modulo PBW filtration degree `d - 1`, filtration degree `d`
of `U(L)` is spanned by the ordered monomials of degree `d` in `bA`. In the induced module
`U(L) ⊗_{U(B)} R_χ` this is the spanning half of the identification of its associated graded with
the symmetric algebra of `L / B`. -/
theorem _root_.LieAlgebra.LieCharacter.pbwFiltration_le_span_pbwMonomial_sup {A : Submodule R L}
    (hA : IsCompl A (B : Submodule R L)) {ιA : Type w₁} [LinearOrder ιA] (bA : Basis ιA R A)
    [Module.Free R B] (d : ℕ) :
    pbwFiltration R L d ≤ Submodule.span R ((fun α : ιA →₀ ℕ ↦
        pbwMonomial R L (fun i ↦ (bA i : L)) (α.toMultiset.sort (· ≤ ·))) '' {α | α.degree = d}) ⊔
      ((Submodule.span U (Set.range fun x : B ↦
        _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (x : L) - algebraMap R U (χ x))).restrictScalars R ⊔
          pbwFiltrationPrevious R L d) := by
  let _ : LinearOrder (Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex R B) := IsWellOrder.linearOrder WellOrderingRel
  let bB := Module.Free.chooseBasis R B
  intro s hs
  rw [LieSubalgebra.mem_pbwFiltration_iff_relativePBWBasis_repr B hA bA bB] at hs
  rw [← (B.relativePBWBasis hA bA bB).linearCombination_repr s, Finsupp.linearCombination_apply]
  refine Submodule.finsuppSum_mem _ _ _ _ fun p hp ↦ Submodule.smul_mem _ _ ?_
  obtain ⟨α, β⟩ := p
  have hdeg : α.degree + β.degree ≤ d := hs _ (Finsupp.mem_support_iff.2 hp)
  -- Split off the character value of the subalgebra monomial, which leaves an element of the left
  -- ideal.
  set r := map R B.incl (bB.pbwBasis β)
  set c := _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.lift R χ (bB.pbwBasis β)
  have hsplit : B.relativePBWBasis hA bA bB (α, β) =
      complementMonomial bA α * (r - algebraMap R U c) + c • complementMonomial bA α := by
    rw [LieSubalgebra.relativePBWBasis_apply, ← complementMonomial, mul_sub, Algebra.smul_def,
      Algebra.commutes c, sub_add_cancel]
  rw [hsplit]
  refine add_mem (Submodule.mem_sup_right (Submodule.mem_sup_left ?_)) (Submodule.smul_mem _ _ ?_)
  · exact Submodule.smul_mem _ _
      (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.map_sub_algebraMap_lift_mem_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap
        B χ _)
  · rcases (Nat.le_of_add_right_le hdeg).eq_or_lt with hα | hα
    · exact Submodule.mem_sup_left (Submodule.subset_span ⟨α, hα, (rfl)⟩)
    · obtain ⟨k, rfl⟩ := Nat.exists_eq_add_of_lt hα
      refine Submodule.mem_sup_right (Submodule.mem_sup_right ?_)
      rw [pbwFiltrationPrevious_succ]
      exact pbwFiltration_mono R L (by omega) (complementMonomial_mem_pbwFiltration bA α)

end Induced

section Free

variable (B : LieSubalgebra R L) (χ : LieCharacter R B)

/-- **A character of a Lie subalgebra generates a proper left ideal.** If the Lie subalgebra `B`
of `L` has a complement `A` and both are free, then for every character `χ` of `B` the elements
`ι x - χ x` of `U(L)`, for `x : B`, generate a proper left ideal of `U(L)`. Equivalently, the
induced module `U(L) ⊗_{U(B)} R_χ` is nonzero. -/
theorem span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap_ne_top_of_isCompl [Nontrivial R] {A : Submodule R L}
    (hA : IsCompl A (B : Submodule R L)) [Module.Free R A] [Module.Free R B] :
    Submodule.span U (Set.range fun x : B ↦
      _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι R (x : L) - algebraMap R U (χ x)) ≠ ⊤ := by
  let _ : LinearOrder (Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex R A) := IsWellOrder.linearOrder WellOrderingRel
  let _ : LinearOrder (Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex R B) := IsWellOrder.linearOrder WellOrderingRel
  exact span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap_ne_top_of_basis B hA (Module.Free.chooseBasis R A)
    (Module.Free.chooseBasis R B) χ

end Free

section Field

/-- **A character of a Lie subalgebra generates a proper left ideal, over a field.** For every
Lie subalgebra `B` of a Lie algebra `L` over a field and every character `χ` of `B`, the elements
`ι x - χ x` of `U(L)`, for `x : B`, generate a proper left ideal of `U(L)`. -/
theorem span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap_ne_top {K : Type u} {L : Type v} [Field K] [LieRing L]
    [LieAlgebra K L] (B : LieSubalgebra K L) (χ : LieCharacter K B) :
    Submodule.span (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) (Set.range fun x : B ↦
      _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K (x : L) -
        algebraMap K (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) (χ x)) ≠ ⊤ := by
  obtain ⟨A, hA⟩ := Submodule.exists_isCompl (B : Submodule K L)
  exact span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap_ne_top_of_isCompl B χ hA.symm

/-- **Degree-one elements of the induced relations, over a field.** For every Lie subalgebra `B`
of a Lie algebra `L` over a field and every character `χ` of `B`, the element `ι x - a` lies in the
left ideal generated by the elements `ι y - χ y`, for `y : B`, exactly when `x` lies in `B` and
`a = χ x`. -/
theorem ι_sub_algebraMap_mem_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap_iff {K : Type u} {L : Type v} [Field K]
    [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra K L] {B : LieSubalgebra K L} (χ : LieCharacter K B) {x : L} {a : K} :
    _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K x -
        algebraMap K (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) a ∈
        Submodule.span (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) (Set.range fun y : B ↦
          _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K (y : L) -
            algebraMap K (_root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L) (χ y)) ↔
      ∃ y : B, (y : L) = x ∧ χ y = a := by
  obtain ⟨A, hA⟩ := Submodule.exists_isCompl (B : Submodule K L)
  exact ι_sub_algebraMap_mem_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap_iff_of_isCompl χ hA.symm

end Field

section Intersection

variable {K : Type u} {L : Type v} [Field K] [LieRing L] [LieAlgebra K L]

local notation "UK" => _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra K L

/-- **Ordered monomials stay independent in the induced module, degreewise.** Let `B` be a Lie
subalgebra of a Lie algebra over a field, `χ` a character of `B`, and `v` a family which is
linearly independent on a set `s` of indices and whose span on `s` meets `B` only in zero. Then
the ordered monomials of degree `d` in the vectors `v i`, `i ∈ s`, are linearly independent
modulo the left ideal generated by the elements `ι x - χ x`, for `x : B`, and filtration degree
`d - 1`. This is the independence half of the identification of the associated graded of the
induced module `U(L) ⊗_{U(B)} K_χ` with the symmetric algebra of `L / B`. -/
theorem _root_.LieAlgebra.LieCharacter.linearIndepOn_mkQ_pbwMonomial {B : LieSubalgebra K L}
    (χ : LieCharacter K B)
    {ι : Type*} [LinearOrder ι] {v : ι → L} {s : Set ι} (hv : LinearIndepOn K v s)
    (hvB : Disjoint (Submodule.span K (v '' s)) (B : Submodule K L)) (d : ℕ) :
    LinearIndepOn K (fun α : ι →₀ ℕ ↦ ((Submodule.span UK (Set.range fun x : B ↦
        _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K (x : L) - algebraMap K UK (χ x))).restrictScalars K ⊔
          pbwFiltrationPrevious K L d).mkQ (pbwMonomial K L v (α.toMultiset.sort (· ≤ ·))))
      {α | α.degree = d ∧ ↑α.support ⊆ s} := by
  -- A basis of the span `V` of the family, extended by a basis of a complement `A'` of `V ⊔ B`,
  -- is a basis of the complement `V ⊔ A'` of `B`.
  set V := Submodule.span K (Set.range fun i : s ↦ v i)
  let bV : Basis s K V := Basis.span hv
  rw [Set.image_eq_range] at hvB
  obtain ⟨A', hA'⟩ := Submodule.exists_isCompl (V ⊔ (B : Submodule K L))
  let f : V × A' →ₗ[K] L := V.subtype.coprod A'.subtype
  have hf : Function.Injective f := by
    rw [← LinearMap.ker_eq_bot, LinearMap.ker_coprod_of_disjoint_range, Submodule.ker_subtype,
      Submodule.ker_subtype, Submodule.prod_bot]
    simpa using hA'.disjoint.mono_left le_sup_left
  have hA : IsCompl (LinearMap.range f) (B : Submodule K L) := by
    rw [LinearMap.range_coprod, Submodule.range_subtype, Submodule.range_subtype]
    refine ⟨(hvB.symm.disjoint_sup_right_of_disjoint_sup_left ?_).symm, ?_⟩
    · rw [sup_comm]
      exact hA'.disjoint
    · rw [codisjoint_iff, sup_right_comm]
      exact hA'.codisjoint.eq_top
  let _ : LinearOrder (Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex K A') := IsWellOrder.linearOrder WellOrderingRel
  let _ : LinearOrder (Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex K B) := IsWellOrder.linearOrder WellOrderingRel
  let bB := Module.Free.chooseBasis K B
  let bA := ((bV.prod (Module.Free.chooseBasis K A')).map
    (LinearEquiv.ofInjective f hf)).reindex (toLex : s ⊕ _ ≃ _)
  have hbA (i : s) : (bA (toLex (Sum.inl i)) : L) = v i := by
    simp [bA, f, bV, Basis.span_apply hv i]
  classical
  -- Exponent vectors supported on `s` are carried to exponent vectors of the extended basis.
  let inl : s ↪o s ⊕ₗ Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex K A' :=
    ⟨⟨fun i ↦ toLex (Sum.inl i), fun _ _ h ↦ Sum.inl_injective (toLex.injective h)⟩,
      Sum.Lex.inl_le_inl_iff⟩
  let extend : (ι →₀ ℕ) → (s ⊕ₗ Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex K A' →₀ ℕ) :=
    fun α ↦ (α.subtypeDomain (· ∈ s)).mapDomain inl
  have hsub {α : ι →₀ ℕ} (hα : ↑α.support ⊆ s) :
      (α.subtypeDomain (· ∈ s)).mapDomain (OrderEmbedding.subtype (· ∈ s)) = α := by
    have h := Finsupp.extendDomain_subtypeDomain α (P := (· ∈ s)) fun _ ha ↦ hα ha
    rwa [Finsupp.extendDomain_eq_embDomain_subtype, Finsupp.embDomain_eq_mapDomain] at h
  have hmon {α : ι →₀ ℕ} (hα : ↑α.support ⊆ s) :
      complementMonomial bA (extend α) = pbwMonomial K L v (α.toMultiset.sort (· ≤ ·)) := by
    have h := pbwMonomial_sort_toMultiset_mapDomain K L (OrderEmbedding.subtype (· ∈ s)) v
      (α.subtypeDomain (· ∈ s))
    rw [hsub hα] at h
    rw [complementMonomial, pbwMonomial_sort_toMultiset_mapDomain K L inl, h]
    congr 1
    exact funext hbA
  have hdeg {α : ι →₀ ℕ} (hα : ↑α.support ⊆ s) : (extend α).degree = α.degree := by
    rw [Finsupp.degree_mapDomain, ← Finsupp.degree_mapDomain (OrderEmbedding.subtype (· ∈ s)),
      hsub hα]
  have hinj {α γ : ι →₀ ℕ} (hα : ↑α.support ⊆ s) (hγ : ↑γ.support ⊆ s)
      (h : extend α = extend γ) : α = γ := by
    rw [← hsub hα, ← hsub hγ, Finsupp.mapDomain_injective inl.injective h]
  -- The character form of the extended exponent vector of `γ` reads off the coefficient of `γ`.
  rw [linearIndepOn_iff]
  intro l hl hl0
  have hl0' : Finsupp.linearCombination K (fun α : ι →₀ ℕ ↦
      pbwMonomial K L v (α.toMultiset.sort (· ≤ ·))) l ∈
        (Submodule.span UK (Set.range fun x : B ↦ _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K (x : L) -
          algebraMap K UK (χ x))).restrictScalars K ⊔ pbwFiltrationPrevious K L d := by
    rw [← Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero, ← Submodule.mkQ_apply, Finsupp.apply_linearCombination]
    exact hl0
  ext γ
  by_cases hγ : γ ∈ {α : ι →₀ ℕ | α.degree = d ∧ ↑α.support ⊆ s}
  swap
  · exact Finsupp.notMem_support_iff.1 fun h ↦ hγ (hl h)
  obtain ⟨hγd, hγs⟩ := hγ
  have h0 : characterForm B hA bA bB χ (extend γ) (Finsupp.linearCombination K
      (fun α : ι →₀ ℕ ↦ pbwMonomial K L v (α.toMultiset.sort (· ≤ ·))) l) = 0 := by
    obtain ⟨j, hj, z, hz, hjz⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.1 hl0'
    rw [← hjz, map_add, characterForm_eq_zero_of_mem_span B hA bA bB χ _ hj,
      characterForm_eq_zero_of_mem_pbwFiltrationPrevious B hA bA bB χ
        (by rwa [hdeg hγs, hγd]), add_zero]
  rw [Finsupp.linearCombination_apply, map_finsuppSum, Finsupp.sum,
    Finset.sum_eq_single γ] at h0
  · simpa [← hmon hγs, characterForm_complementMonomial] using h0
  · intro α hα hne
    have hne' : extend α ≠ extend γ := fun h ↦ hne (hinj (hl hα).2 hγs h)
    rw [map_smul, ← hmon (hl hα).2, characterForm_complementMonomial]
    simp [hne']
  · intro hγ'
    rw [Finsupp.notMem_support_iff.1 hγ', zero_smul, map_zero]

/-- **Intersections of induced relations along a directed family.** Let `B i` be a nonempty
downward-directed family of Lie subalgebras of a Lie algebra `L` over a field, and let `χ` be a
linear form on `L` vanishing on the brackets of each `B i`, so that it restricts to a character of
each `B i` and of their intersection. Then the left ideals of `U(L)` generated by the elements
`ι x - χ x`, for `x ∈ B i`, intersect in the left ideal generated by the same elements for `x` in
the intersection of the `B i`. -/
theorem iInf_span_range_ι_sub_algebraMap {ι : Type*} [Nonempty ι] {B : ι → LieSubalgebra K L}
    (hB : Directed (· ≥ ·) B) (χ : L →ₗ[K] K) (hχ : ∀ i, ∀ x ∈ B i, ∀ y ∈ B i, χ ⁅x, y⁆ = 0) :
    ⨅ i, Submodule.span UK (Set.range fun x : B i ↦
        _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K (x : L) - algebraMap K UK (χ x)) =
      Submodule.span UK (Set.range fun x : ↥(⨅ i, B i) ↦
        _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K (x : L) - algebraMap K UK (χ x)) := by
  have hmem {x : L} : x ∈ ⨅ i, B i ↔ ∀ i, x ∈ B i := by
    rw [← SetLike.mem_coe, ← sInf_range, LieSubalgebra.coe_sInf]
    simp
  set Binf := ⨅ i, B i
  set J : LieSubalgebra K L → Submodule UK UK := fun B' ↦ Submodule.span UK
    (Set.range fun x : B' ↦ _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K (x : L) - algebraMap K UK (χ x))
  have hJ (i : ι) : J Binf ≤ J (B i) := Submodule.span_mono <| by
    rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
    exact ⟨⟨x, hmem.1 x.2 i⟩, rfl⟩
  refine le_antisymm ?_ (le_iInf hJ)
  have hχinf : ∀ x ∈ Binf, ∀ y ∈ Binf, χ ⁅x, y⁆ = 0 := fun x hx y hy ↦
    hχ (Classical.arbitrary ι) x (hmem.1 hx _) y (hmem.1 hy _)
  -- An ordered basis of a complement of the intersection.
  obtain ⟨C, hC⟩ := Submodule.exists_isCompl (Binf : Submodule K L)
  let _ : LinearOrder (Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex K C) := IsWellOrder.linearOrder WellOrderingRel
  let bC := Module.Free.chooseBasis K C
  -- Induction on the PBW filtration degree.
  suffices key : ∀ d, ∀ x ∈ pbwFiltrationPrevious K L d, (∀ i, x ∈ J (B i)) → x ∈ J Binf by
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨d, hd⟩ := exists_mem_pbwFiltration K L x
    exact key (d + 1) x (by rwa [pbwFiltrationPrevious_succ]) ((Submodule.mem_iInf _).1 hx)
  intro d
  induction d with
  | zero =>
    intro x hx _
    rw [pbwFiltrationPrevious_zero, Submodule.mem_bot] at hx
    exact hx ▸ zero_mem _
  | succ d ih =>
    intro x hx hxJ
    rw [pbwFiltrationPrevious_succ] at hx
    -- Modulo `J Binf` and lower degree, `x` is a combination `y` of degree-`d` monomials in `bC`.
    have hG :=
      (Binf.restrictCharacter χ hχinf).pbwFiltration_le_span_pbwMonomial_sup hC.symm bC d hx
    simp only [LieSubalgebra.restrictCharacter_apply] at hG
    obtain ⟨y, hy, w, hw, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.1 hG
    obtain ⟨c, hc, rfl⟩ := (Finsupp.mem_span_image_iff_linearCombination K).1 hy
    -- The finitely many basis vectors occurring in `y` span a subspace disjoint from some `B i`.
    set S : Finset (Module.Free.ChooseBasisIndex K C) := c.support.biUnion Finsupp.support
    set V := Submodule.span K ((fun j ↦ (bC j : L)) '' S)
    have hVC : V ≤ C := Submodule.span_le.2 <| by
      rintro _ ⟨j, -, rfl⟩
      exact (bC j).2
    have : FiniteDimensional K V := FiniteDimensional.span_of_finite K (S.finite_toSet.image _)
    have hdisj : Disjoint V (⨅ j, (B j : Submodule K L)) :=
      Submodule.disjoint_def.2 fun x hx hx' ↦ Submodule.disjoint_def.1
        (hC.disjoint.symm.mono_left hVC) x hx (hmem.2 fun j ↦ (Submodule.mem_iInf _).1 hx' j)
    obtain ⟨i, hVi⟩ := Submodule.exists_disjoint_of_directed V (fun j ↦ (B j : Submodule K L))
      (hB.mono_comp (· ≥ ·) fun _ _ h ↦ (LieSubalgebra.toSubmodule_le_toSubmodule _ _).2 h) hdisj
    have hindep := ((B i).restrictCharacter χ (hχ i)).linearIndepOn_mkQ_pbwMonomial
      (v := fun j ↦ (bC j : L)) (s := ↑S)
      ((bC.linearIndependent.map' C.subtype C.ker_subtype).comp _ Subtype.val_injective) hVi d
    have hJi : Submodule.span UK (Set.range fun x : B i ↦ _root_.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra.ι K
        (x : L) - algebraMap K UK ((B i).restrictCharacter χ (hχ i) x)) = J (B i) := by
      simp only [LieSubalgebra.restrictCharacter_apply, J]
    rw [hJi] at hindep
    -- Hence `y = 0`.
    have hc0 : c = 0 := by
      refine linearIndepOn_iff.1 hindep c (fun α hα ↦ ⟨hc hα, fun j hj ↦ ?_⟩) ?_
      · exact Finset.mem_biUnion.2 ⟨α, hα, hj⟩
      have hx' : _ ∈ (J (B i)).restrictScalars K ⊔ pbwFiltrationPrevious K L d :=
        Submodule.mem_sup_left ((Submodule.restrictScalars_mem K _ _).2 (hxJ i))
      have hmem' := sub_mem hx' (sup_le_sup_right (Submodule.restrictScalars_mono K (hJ i)) _ hw)
      rw [add_sub_cancel_right, ← Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero, ← Submodule.mkQ_apply,
        Finsupp.apply_linearCombination] at hmem'
      exact hmem'
    subst hc0
    rw [map_zero, zero_add] at hxJ ⊢
    obtain ⟨j, hj, z, hz, rfl⟩ := Submodule.mem_sup.1 hw
    refine add_mem hj (ih z hz fun i ↦ ?_)
    simpa using sub_mem (hxJ i) (hJ i hj)

end Intersection

end TauCeti.UniversalEnvelopingAlgebra
